# SECRETS TEMPLATE, one for every env: committed with placeholders only, never real values.
# _deploy/scripts/install.sh <env> renders it to /etc/pace-<env>.env on the host
# (mode 0640, group = that env's service user), filling {{PG_*}} from
# _deploy/envs/pace-<env>.env. Then edit in the real passwords (every CHANGEME);
# install.sh won't start the service until they're gone. systemd loads that file after
# the settings file, so a key set in both takes this file's value. Anything that isn't
# a secret goes in _deploy/envs/pace-<env>.env instead. See README.md → Config files.

# Async SQLAlchemy URL; tables live in the `pace` schema. User, host, port
# and database come from the settings file (sbx → synveon_dev, uat/prod → synveon).
# Replace CHANGEME with that user's password.
POSTGRES_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://{{PG_USER}}:CHANGEME@{{PG_HOST}}:{{PG_PORT}}/{{PG_DATABASE}}

# SQL Server password — OPTIONAL (reports, /api/reports/*). Only needed when SQL
# Server is enabled (SQLSERVER_HOST set in the settings file). Uncomment + set to
# enable; left commented, /api/reports/* returns 503.
# SQLSERVER_PASSWORD=CHANGEME

# Do NOT set AUTH_DISABLED here — deployed envs must validate real tokens.
